       ggeettssoocckknnaammee() returns the current address to which the socket _s_o_c_k_f_d is
       bound,  in  the buffer pointed to by _a_d_d_r.  The _a_d_d_r_l_e_n argument should
       be initialized to indicate the amount of space (in bytes) pointed to by
       _a_d_d_r.  On return it contains the actual size of the socket address.

       The returned address is truncated if the buffer provided is too  small;
       in  this case, _a_d_d_r_l_e_n will return a value greater than was supplied to
       the call.

